{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Second plan review 2026-10-19 (BLOCK, 1 move), confirmed on f147e08242f: AC2's packaging predicate (`grep -c 'evals/'` over the wheel listing, `grep -c '/evals/'` over the sdist) could never print 0, because the wheel ships the whole `src/rebar` tree (`pyproject.toml:367`) including the Python package `rebar/llm/evals/`, and the sdist includes it too (`:398`). The patterns are now anchored to the archive root (`^evals/` after stripping the sdist's top directory), so only a top-level corpus directory matches. The AC also now states why the check exists: both build targets already exclude a top-level `evals/`, so it guards against a future include change rather than the current state."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792392568651111746,"uuid":"42774c2a-b347-4b7d-a556-a3a07fd02eac"}